<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26409" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δῐδασκᾰλ-ικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of</i> or <i>for teaching,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philol.
					11
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄργανον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Cra.</u>
					388b
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόγοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Mem.</u>
					1.2.21
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πειθὼ δ. περί τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Grg.</u>
					453e
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				455a
			</span></i>: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ -κή</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέχνη</span>) <i>the faculty of giving
				instruction,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Sph.</u>
				231b
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ -κόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					813b
				</span></i>
			; so, in disparagement, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ πρεσβυτικὸν
				καὶ δ.</span>
			<i>the didactic manner</i> of old age, of Isocrates, <i><span class="en">
				Hermog.
				<u>Id.</u>
				2.11
			</span></i>: 
				Comp.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ώτερος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Metaph.</u>
					982a13
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Cra.</u>
					388c
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				6.3.5
			</span></i>: 
				Comp.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ώτερον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Dioph.
					1p.474T.
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hermog.
				<u>Inv.</u>
				1.1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κή</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁμολογίἀ, ἡ,</span>
			<i>contract of apprenticeship,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				POxy.
				275.34
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(i A. D.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> Gramm., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τόπος δ.,</span>
			<i>locus classicus,</i> Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				5.857
			</span></i>.</div>
